9
00:32:28,695 --> 00:32:34,695
Don't Kill It is a 2016 American comedy horror film
directed and edited by Mike Mendez.

10
00:36:05,217 --> 00:36:11,217
Written by Dan Berk and Robert Olsen, it stars Dolph Lundgren as Jebediah Woodley, a demon hunter
who travels to Mississippi in the hopes of destroying an ancient, homicidal demon.

11
00:39:41,739 --> 00:39:47,739
Kristina Klebe, Tony Bentley, James Chalke, and Miles
Doleac appear in supporting roles.

12
00:43:18,260 --> 00:43:24,260
Mendez was attached to direct for over four years.

13
00:46:54,782 --> 00:47:00,782
Originally set in Alaska, once green-lit the script was altered and
filming moved to Mississippi over financial concerns.

14
00:50:31,304 --> 00:50:37,304
The budget was less than $1 million, with $15,000 of it
raised via the crowdfunding website Indiegogo.

15
00:54:07,826 --> 00:54:13,826
Lundgren was cast around 9–10 months before filming commenced,
whilst Klebe only had one-to-two weeks notice.

16
00:57:44,347 --> 00:57:50,347
After being postponed twice, principal photography commenced over the
2015 Christmas holiday season in Lexington, Mississippi.

17
01:01:20,869 --> 01:01:26,869
Filming concluded after 17 days of shooting, with the film having its premiere
at the Fantasy Filmfest in Hamburg, Germany, on August 27, 2016.

18
01:04:57,391 --> 01:05:03,391
This was followed by the North American premiere on September
26, 2016, at Fantastic Fest in Austin, Texas.

19
01:08:33,913 --> 01:08:39,913
A limited theatrical release followed on March 3, 2017, via AMC Theatres.

20
01:12:10,434 --> 01:12:16,434
Opening to mostly positive reviews, Noel Murray of the Los Angeles Times, described
Don't Kill It as one of Lundgren's "most entertaining movies in years."

21
01:15:46,956 --> 01:15:52,956
The film explores themes of fbi, gore, demon, evil, demonic possession.

22
01:19:23,478 --> 01:19:29,478
The tone is dark.
